  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 102 AM MDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nDry and cool temperatures are expected today. Highs today will \nbe a few degrees below normal. Overnight lows going into Monday \nmorning will be chilly once again and marginal for frost \nadvisories in the Snake River Plain. On Tuesday, a low pressure \nsystem over Nevada will weaken and lift northward into our \nregion. Models are developing a few showers with this system but\nlittle if any qpf. This system pulls away from our area by \nWednesday leaving us with dry conditions for the remainder of \nthe week. Temperatures will climb above normal for the second \nhalf of the week with many areas seeing temps in the upper 70s \nto low 80s.",
